<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolf II of Holstein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1128">1128</a>–<a href="/years/1164">1164</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolf II of Holstein was count of Holstein and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stormarn">Stormarn</a> from 1130, of the house of Schauenburg. He pushed German settlement into Slavic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wagria">Wagria</a> and in 1143 founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, which later passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>. He was killed fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obotrites">Obotrites</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-verchen">Battle of Verchen</a> in 1164.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adolf-ii-of-holstein.jpg" alt="Adolf II of Holstein" width="320" height="600" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adolf_II._von_Schauenburg,_Holstein_und_Storman_(1128-1164).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
